# The document + data toolchain, as DECLARED. These are the packages we intend to ship and support;
# everything they drag in is resolved into requirements.txt, which is what the image installs.
#
# Edit this file to add or bump a package, then regenerate the lock:
#
#   scripts/compile-python-deps.sh
#
# Why the lock exists: PyPI has no distro-style freeze, so a transitive dep can publish any day.
# Recording the closure in ENVIRONMENT.lock catches that drift, but only AFTER it has already landed
# in a build — which blocks whatever unrelated change happened to be in flight. Pinning the closure
# moves the upgrade to a deliberate, reviewed diff instead. (apt stays recorded-not-pinned on
# purpose: Debian stable freezes it, so it doesn't churn the same way.)

